# Keep the working tree byte-identical on every platform.
#
# Without this, git's core.autocrlf rewrites text files on Windows checkout,
# and the suite then compares fixtures it wrote with LF against files checked
# out with CRLF. The product itself normalises line endings when it parses
# (see tests/unit/line-endings.test.ts), but the repository should not be the
# thing introducing the variation.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Shell scripts must keep LF even on Windows: CRLF makes a shebang unusable.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Binary-ish artifacts git should never touch.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.gif binary
*.tgz binary
